│ RESULTS One hundred forty-nine patients (48 received aprotinin, 50 desmopressin, 51 placebo) were included. Blood    │
│ loss and transfusion requirements were recorded and levels of Factor VIII coagulant activity, von Willebrand\'s      │
│ factor, thrombin-antithrombin complexes, and D-dimer were measured. Overall blood loss was 195 +/- 146 ml/m2 in the  │
│ aprotinin group, 400 +/- 192 ml/m2 in the desmopressin group, and 489 +/- 361 ml/m2 in the placebo group (95%        │
│ confidence intervals: difference between desmopressin and aprotinin 98 to 312 ml/m2, p < 0.001; difference between   │
│ placebo and aprotinin 190 to 398 ml/m2, p < 0.001). Twenty-six percent of patients treated with aprotinin, 66% of    │
│ those treated with desmopressin, and 56% of those treated with placebo were given transfusion (95% confidence        │
