substantially higher blood loss and transfusion requirements than untreated control patients. INTERPRETATION Patients   
identified with hemoSTATUS as being at increased risk of excessive bleeding after cardiac surgery can benefit from      
administration of desmopressin. Further studies are, however, needed to confirm these findings as well as to identify   
the mechanism of action and safety of desmopressin in the clinical setting."}, {"study_index": 8, "title": "The effect  
of 6% hydroxyethyl starch and desmopressin infusion on von Willebrand factor: ristocetin cofactor activity", "abstract":
"Hydroxyethyl starch is commonly used as a plasma volume expander in the surgical patient. Although it is generally     
