  blocks in a randomized double-blind placebo-controlled parallel group trial on the effects of DDAVP on postoperative  
  bleeding after uncomplicated coronary artery bypass operations. After termination of extra-corporeal circulation,     
  DDAVP (0.3 microgram/kg body wt) or its vehicle was infused into a peripheral vein throughout 15 minutes. The         
  increase in factor VIII coagulant activity after infusion did not differ between the groups but there was a           
  significantly larger increase in vWF:Ag levels in DDAVP-treated patients. The aggregatory response to                 
  adenosine-diphosphate (ADP) and ristocetin showed a normal pattern and was not significantly different between the    
